            <ArticleTitle>Carboplatin hypersensitivity presenting as coronary vasospasm - a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>429-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 68-year-old female patient with advanced ovarian carcinoma collapsed whilst receiving a carboplatin and cyclophosphamide infusion. This reaction was considered to fit with coronary vasospasm. Hypersensitivity to carboplatin is a rare but real complication of therapy and should be considered in patients presenting with hyperacute changes on ECG whilst receiving carboplatin therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
